{"ts":"2026-08-25T05:07:23.485Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-5.6-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9b054e739855a3b67742faac","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-5.6-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-a8zm","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-a8zm","lineage:pm-6x7o","lineage:pm-96h7","lineage:pm-33cw","lineage:pm-doxj"]}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"## Decision questions\n\n1. Canonical version and exact supported legacy versions.\n2. STDIO compatibility probe behavior when server/discover is unknown to an older client.\n3. Whether protocol support remains hand-rolled, adopts an official SDK, or isolates schema-derived wire contracts behind the public pm SDK.\n4. Streamable HTTP deployment and authorization scope.\n5. Removal or adapter policy for initialize, notifications/initialized, ping, logging/setLevel, roots changes, resource subscriptions, SSE resumability, and deprecated features.\n6. Capability and extension negotiation when a caller omits or conflicts with request metadata.\n7. Rollout, metrics, sunset criteria, and rollback without mutable history.\n\n## Preferred direction\n\nUse the official schema as the normative wire contract, keep transport-neutral semantics in the public pm SDK, make 2026-07-28 the default, and retain only explicitly tested compatibility adapters that do not recreate protocol-level sessions."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-sqvshj"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"ADR: MCP 2026-07-28 is canonical and legacy interoperability is a bounded stateless adapter, not connection-local session state"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Choose the protocol-version, transport, compatibility, and dependency strategy for replacing the 2025-06-18 initialize handshake without preserving forbidden session semantics."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Decision"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["adr","area:mcp","compatibility","deprecation","protocol-versioning","stateless"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-25T05:07:23.485Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-25T05:07:23.485Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/deadline","value":"2026-09-15T00:00:00.000Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The accepted decision names canonical and supported legacy protocol versions plus a sunset policy; The decision resolves hand-rolled versus official-SDK usage while preserving the public pm SDK as the policy boundary; STDIO and Streamable HTTP negotiation, discovery, compatibility probes, and unsupported-version errors are specified; Every removed or deprecated feature has an explicit remove, adapt, or migrate disposition with security rationale; Rollout telemetry, negative controls, rollback, and released-artifact gates are defined before implementation starts"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/goal","value":"Interoperable current MCP without ambiguous dual semantics"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/objective","value":"Approve one explicit compatibility policy for 2026-07-28 core behavior, legacy clients, transports, extensions, and deprecations"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/value","value":"Implementation teams can migrate once against a stable architecture and test matrix"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/why_now","value":"Every downstream protocol child depends on whether initialize, ping, sessions, server-initiated requests, and legacy HTTP behavior remain adapters or are removed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-rs9vry"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"critical"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-kl11","kind":"supersedes","created_at":"2026-08-25T05:07:23.485Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-pif3","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-25T05:07:23.485Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-25T05:07:23.485Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses for MCP protocol ADR 2026-07-28 stateless compatibility initialize removal and legacy adapters. pm-pif3 covers the old dependency-free implementation choice and pm-kl11 covers the old handshake test; neither decides the new revision."}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"9953e58e9f64b03f9e1c3280d22ecd5eba7cab1a31a9fe03f142e6b11ba7866a","item_hash_version":2,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
